WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.762
(slow, tender music)

00:00:03.762 --> 00:00:05.660
(rhythmic beeping)

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.193
- The surgeon is real.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.453
The tools are real.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.093
The surgery is real.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.133
The patient is artificial.

00:00:23.404 --> 00:00:26.060
(playful music)

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.930
I took what I learned
from special effects,

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:33.517
and now I apply it to helping
kids here at the hospital.

00:00:38.931 --> 00:00:42.431
(playful xylophone music)

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:50.330
My name is Gregory Loan,
and I'm a senior simulation

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.620
engineer at Boston Children's Hospital.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.610
I make artificial patients
to allow real doctors

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:00.923
to practice procedures to
improve health outcomes for kids.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.850
I do not think that I could do this work

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.520
without having had the experiences

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.263
that I had in special effects.

00:01:13.943 --> 00:01:15.460
While I was working in special effects,

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.830
I got the opportunity to build dinosaurs

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.980
for the Jurassic Park theme parks

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.050
and magical creatures for Harry Potter

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:25.420
and all kinds of wonderful things

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.113
to bring that experience
to life for people.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.720
I ultimately left special effects

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.750
to go focus in on robotics,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.700
which is my other passion in life.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.100
The best part is now I
combine special effects,

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.400
robotics, and engineering, and medicine

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.063
into a package that helps people.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.300
I make simulation models.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.480
Some of them are really low tech,

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.480
like an arm that you can inject
or practice line placement,

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:04.470
all the way up to and including

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:09.140
gunshot wound patients and
advanced surgical techniques,

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.603
like cleft lip repair.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.280
At the end of the day, I know that

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.080
my contribution helps kids

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.610
because the creations that we make here

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.113
go towards saving children's lives.

00:02:23.338 --> 00:02:26.007
- [Surgeon] And it looks
like we're about done.

00:02:26.007 --> 00:02:28.840
(uplifting music)

00:02:30.898 --> 00:02:33.981
(electronic pinging)

